# gstack skills to leave unregistered.
#
# Upstream gstack ships every skill it has. Each registered skill spends
# description text in every agent session's skill budget, so this list keeps
# only the ones this fleet actually uses.
#
# One name per line. Bare (`browse`) and prefixed (`gstack-browse`) both work.
# `#` starts a comment. A name matching no upstream skill is warned about on
# `dot update`, not silently ignored. Format and validation are owned by the
# gstack-register provider; this file contains only dotfiles policy choices.
#
# Read from the provider's normal XDG config path. Changes apply on the next
# `dot update` or explicit `gstack-register sync`.

# iOS — no iOS or SwiftUI development on this fleet.
ios-clean
ios-design-review
ios-fix
ios-qa
ios-sync

# Browser-driven web QA — no web frontend work, so the headless browser and
# its scrape/record helpers go unused.
#
# `connect-chrome` and `open-gstack-browser` are two upstream directories that
# both declare `name: open-gstack-browser`, so they generate the same
# `gstack-open-gstack-browser` link. Matching is by directory name, so both
# have to be listed or the un-excluded one regenerates the link.
benchmark
browse
connect-chrome
open-gstack-browser
pair-agent
qa
qa-only
scrape
setup-browser-cookies
skillify

# Context and memory — this fleet already has a durable memory store, and a
# second one only adds ambiguity about where a fact belongs.
context-restore
context-save
learn
setup-gbrain
sync-gbrain

# Edit guardrails — pre-tool hooks already enforce edit boundaries and warn on
# destructive commands. Two guard layers that can disagree is worse than one.
careful
freeze
guard
unfreeze
